course: medicine
lesson: 69
title: Girls' and boys' teams
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Josh in Bristol sneers «You kick like a girl» at Maya, and her next shot flies into the top corner; how hard you kick comes from technique and practice (plant foot, swing, contact with the laces), not from being a boy or a girl at this age.
explain: Before puberty boys and girls have very similar muscle, speed and strength, so Ruby in Melbourne can be the fastest kid in her class at 9 and tell the boys «Get rekt» («rekt» is gamer slang for totally beaten); bigger differences only come in the teens, when boys make much more of the hormone testosterone.
explain: Nerves are the same chemistry for everyone: the butterflies before a cup final are adrenaline moving blood away from the stomach to the muscles, in boys and girls alike.
explain: Women's sport is big and growing: England's Lionesses won the Euros in 2022 and again in 2025, and the Red Roses won the 2025 Women's Rugby World Cup, while men and boys play netball too, so any sport is open to anyone who loves it.
explain: In England girls can now play in mixed teams right up to under-18, and girls' teams are much easier to find than a few years ago, so the right team is simply the one where you enjoy playing.
fact: Before puberty boys and girls have very similar muscle, speed and strength, and practice matters most.
fact: Bigger differences in strength and speed appear in the teens, when boys make much more testosterone.
fact: How hard and clean you kick a ball depends on technique and practice.
fact: Pre-match butterflies are adrenaline moving blood from the stomach to the muscles, and boys and girls make it the same way.
fact: In England the FA lets boys and girls play in mixed teams up to under-18; the limit used to be under-11.
fact: On 31 July 2022 England's women beat Germany 2–1 after extra time in the Euro final at Wembley in front of 87,192 fans, a record for any Euro final, men's or women's, and millions more watched on TV.
fact: England reached the 2023 Women's World Cup final and then won Euro 2025, beating Spain on penalties (3–1 in the shootout) after a 1–1 draw.
fact: England's Red Roses won the 2025 Women's Rugby World Cup final at Twickenham, beating Canada 33–13.
fact: Men and boys play netball too, and New Zealand has men's netball teams.
fact: Girls in a mixed team who get passed to less get fewer touches and fewer chances to show their skill.
fact: Some girls prefer mixed teams and some prefer girls' teams; it is a choice about fun and friends, not about level.
fact: «It's giving family» is young slang for «it feels like a family»; «our kid» in Yorkshire and the North can mean a brother, sister or cousin.
exercise: What decides how hard a 9-year-old kicks a ball? | Technique and practice | Being a boy or a girl | The colour of their boots | How tall their parents are
exercise: Before puberty, how do boys' and girls' speed and strength compare? | Very similar | Boys are twice as fast | Girls are always weaker | Boys are always stronger
exercise: When do bigger differences in strength usually appear? | In the teens, with more testosterone in boys | At about age 5, when school starts | Never, they stay the same for life | Only in grown-ups over 40
exercise: Josh says Maya «kicks like a girl». What does that line really tell you? | Nothing about how well she kicks | That Maya kicks very badly for her age | That girls can't shoot as hard as boys | That Josh is the best player on the team
exercise: Up to what age can girls play in mixed teams in England now? | Under-18 | Under-8 | Under-11 | Under-21
exercise: Who did the Lionesses beat in the Euro 2022 final? | Germany | Spain | Canada | France
exercise: About how many fans watched that 2022 final at Wembley? | About 87,000 | About 8,700 | About 870 | About 870,000
exercise: How did England win Euro 2025 against Spain? | On penalties after a 1–1 draw | 5–0 in normal time, an easy win | On the away goals rule, after two legs | Spain didn't turn up for the final
exercise: Who won the 2025 Women's Rugby World Cup final? | England's Red Roses | Canada | New Zealand | Nobody, it was cancelled
exercise: Hannah is the only girl and the boys don't pass to her. Why does she seem to do less? | She gets the ball less often | Girls don't want the ball | She is a weaker player | She keeps hiding on the pitch
exercise: Aisha switches to a girls' team. What is that choice about? | Fun and friends, not level | Not being good enough for mixed | A rule forcing her out | Being scared of the boys
exercise: Reuben joins netball. Is netball only for girls? | No, men and boys play it too | Yes, boys are banned from it | Yes, it was made only for girls | No, but only grown men can play
exercise: Olivia has butterflies before the girls' cup final. What are they? | Adrenaline moving blood to her muscles | A sign that girls get more nervous than boys | A tummy bug from the changing room | Her body telling her not to play
exercise: Priyanka wants to play rugby. What's the best advice? | Find a club with a girls' section | Wait until she's grown up and then start | Play only in the garden with her cousin | Choose a «girls' sport» like netball instead
exercise: Ruby runs 60 m in 10 seconds and a boy in 11. How far ahead in time is she? | 1 second | 21 seconds | 10 seconds | 2 seconds
test: «boys are always faster, that's just facts innit». What's true at age 9? | Little difference; practice matters most | Boys are always faster at any age, it's just nature | Girls are faster only at swimming | Boys are faster but only on grass
test: Freya screams «get in!» at the telly in 2022. Her uncle: «nobody watches women's footy». Put him right. | A record Euro crowd and millions on TV watched | Only about 50 people watched that final | It wasn't even shown on telly | Women's football has no crowds
test: «2022 was a fluke, they'll never win again». What happened next? | A 2023 World Cup final and the Euro 2025 title | They never reached a final again | They were knocked out every year | They stopped playing in 2023
test: Reuben's mate: «Netball? That's a girls' sport, bro». What would happen if Reuben listened? | He'd miss a sport he loves for no reason | He'd become a better rugby player by staying away | Netball would ban him anyway | Nothing, netball has no boys' teams
test: The boy watching Olivia: «girls get more nervous, innit». What's the real chemistry? | Everyone gets the same adrenaline rush | Only girls make adrenaline | Boys don't feel nerves at all before a final | Nerves come from wearing a skirt
test: Hannah, 9, in Edinburgh: «Pass it, ya numpties!» What would happen if they passed to whoever's open? | She'd get more touches and chances to show skill | The team would lose every game | She'd stop wanting the ball | The boys would forget how to play
test: Erin's coach says she can stay with the lads next year. Can that be allowed in England? | Yes, mixed teams go up to under-18 | No, girls must leave at under-11 by law | No, mixed football is banned in England | Yes, but only in the garden or the park
test: Priyanka's cousin: «rugby's for lads, our kid». What's actually happening in women's rugby? | England's Red Roses won its 2025 World Cup | It was stopped many years ago | Only a few women play, in secret | Only boys are allowed to play it
test: In a cartoon a girl only wins the race because the boys trip over. What's real at age 9? | She can simply be the fastest | Girls only win when boys fall | Boys always win fair races | Races between them are never allowed
test: Aisha: «honestly, it's giving family». What does she mean about her girls' team? | It feels like a family | It gives her family tickets | Her family is on the team | It costs a family fee
test: Red Roses beat Canada 33–13 in the 2025 final. By how many points did they win? | 20 | 46 | 13 | 33
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the physical capacities of boys and girls prior to puberty? | They are broadly comparable, practice being the principal determinant | Boys invariably exhibit superior speed | Girls invariably exhibit inferior strength | They diverge substantially from the age of five
exam: Pursuant to the regulations of the Football Association in England, state the upper age limit for mixed football. | Under-18 | Under-11 | Under-9 | Under-14
exam: Identify the result of the final of the 2025 Women's Rugby World Cup. | England defeated Canada | Canada defeated England | New Zealand defeated England | The final was abandoned
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning anxiety prior to competition. | Adrenaline is released in an identical manner in boys and girls | Adrenaline is released by girls only | Boys are incapable of experiencing anxiety | Anxiety is caused by the colour of the kit
